{"in":{"id":201,"op":"slates.catalog"}}
{"out":{"id":201,"ok":true,"text":"Slate kit wsp/2, JSX-like text. Pieces (attributes, ! required, (a|b) the only values; <items>):\ncolumn: gap(tight|normal|loose) align; children\ngrid: columns! gap(tight|normal|loose) align; children\nrow: gap(tight|normal|loose) align wrap; children\nsection: title! note collapsible open align onChange; children\ntext: value! tone emphasis mono size(small|normal|large) lines placeholder\nheading: value! level(title|section|label)\nmarkdown: value!\nnumber: label! value! format unit tone note size(normal|large) trend\nmeter: label! value! max note tone format(percent|value|fraction|tokens|bytes|none)\nbars: label! items! key name! value! tone max format(percent|value|none)\nchart: label! items! x value format unit tone height(small|normal|large) stack; <series label! value! tone>\ndiagram: value! label\ntimeline: label! items! name! start end state(done|running|failed|waiting) group now\ntreemap: label! items! name! value! group format\ndonut: label! items! name! value! format unit\nimage: src! caption\nimages: items! src! caption layout(strip|gallery|compare)\nsparkline: label! values! tone\ntable: items! key empty rows; <col title! value! tone emphasis mono align width(fit|fill)> <action label! onPress>\nchecklist: items! key title! done! state(pending|working|done) note editable empty onChange\nfacts: layout(line|grid); <fact label! value! tone emphasis mono>\nstatus: value! tone\nchip: value!\nring: label! value! max format(percent|value|fraction) tone note\noutput: run! label lines wrap\nbutton: label! variant(default|primary|quiet|danger) held note size(normal|small) onPress\ninput: label! value! lines kind(text|number|password) placeholder held mono submit onChange onSubmit\nselect: label! value! placeholder held onChange; <option value! label>\nchoices: label! value! answer held onChange; <option value! label note>\ntoggle: label! value! note held onChange\nempty: title! body\nEvery piece: id, when={cond}; items take when too. tone: default muted good warning bad info accent. emphasis: normal strong quiet. format, where a line lists none: plain tokens bytes percent usd inr duration integer.\nsection, column, grid: pad none tight normal loose; surface=\"inset\" sets the card ground; align start center end, else children fill the width.\nbars compare categories; time is a chart, x in ms or ISO; shares a donut, sizes a treemap, spans on a clock a timeline; a flow is a diagram; a screenshot or plot is an image from its path on the thread's computer, or an https address the person allows.\nSources, read only:\nthread: id title agent model status turns lastTurn cost tokens context changes plan waitingOn subagents[] ...\nusage: account windows[] session week status note ...\ncost: rateUsdPerHour accruedUsd\ntime: now today zone\ngit: branch head ahead behind changed ...\npr: number url state draft branch headSubject mergeable review checks[] word ...\nDeclarations: <value name start> <secret name> <derived name value> <run name cmd env args stdin on timeout every always once confirm then tool resource description> <file name> <when change={$path} or done={$run} do={steps}>\nSteps: set toggle start cancel send steer queue fill open copy pane. Functions: percent pct tokens bytes usd number duration ago until date time weekday plural word upper lower trim short round floor ceil abs min max clamp str num bool concat json lines split replace contains startsWith endsWith orElse exists isNull coalesce if len count sum avg first last at append pluck join. ago(t) \"30s ago\", until(t) \"in 4m\".\nAfter |: where sortBy groupBy take skip count sum min max avg first last pick map distinct flatten join format. $run reads state exit out err json; a secret only .set .len.\nRules:\n1. One <slate>, one root piece, declarations beside it. Give an id to a piece you will change.\n2. prop=\"text\" is literal; prop={formula} reads live data or $values with operators, a ? b : c, [lists], {records} and functions, never methods or =>. A text child with {holes} fills a sentence.\n3. Props are meaning, never style. held is a sentence that disables: bind it to a condition; \"\" or false enables.\n4. A list binds to items; item and index read the row.\n5. A press reaches you only through send(\"literal text\", $path); <when> chains run without you.\n6. Small edit: patch by id, <props id=\"price\" value={$spot.json.v} />; bigger: resend the whole slate with if_version.\n7. Simple and airy unless asked for more: few pieces, one idea per section, short labels, no emoji. Separate things by layout, never by ·, • or |.\n8. One heading per section: its title or a heading, in sentence case, never bold text.\n9. Status and last-checked lines small and muted, beside their subject.\n10. Actions at the end of their row; one primary per section.\n11. mono only for figures, ids, times and paths.\n12. Every live number says its window and unit. Show a run's json fields, never its raw out; times through date(), time() or ago().\n13. Nothing centered but a lone figure or card.\n14. Use the slate tools, never wsp from a shell.\n15. A secret the person types goes in a <secret> input, never a file or the chat. One in a file stays there for the run to read, never you.\n16. A button asked for where the project has no UI goes here: the slate is its UI, and the reply says so.\n<slate title=\"Issue\">\n  <value name=\"id\" start=\"\" />\n  <run name=\"check\" cmd='gh api \"repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/$ID\"' env={{ ID: $id }} />\n  <when change={$id} do={start($check)} />\n  <column>\n    <input label=\"Issue\" value={$id} />\n    <text when={$check.exit == 0}>{$check.json.title}</text>\n    <button label=\"Fix it\" onPress={send(\"Fix this issue.\", $id)} />\n  </column>\n</slate>\nMore: slate_catalog <piece, source, runs, patch, functions, steps, handlers or examples>."}}
